# tally 2.2.1 (#221, 221.10), L §4.4: an undecided interval is HOLE-IMPRECISE wherever one value is needed, "a term of an
# aggregate other than min, max, argmin and argmax". days_between(d0, w) is 4 to 6 days: mean (m) and quantile (q) are
# the window's hole, as sum (sm) was; max (x) gives the interval, a hole only for the print. tally 2.2 refused mean
# (RUN-DOMAIN window(4, 6) + window(4, 6)) and stopped on quantile (REFCORE-NOT-YET, TypeError).
=== agg.tally
model agg
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
index ks = [a, b]
input w: date
input d0: date
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  d0 = 2026-03-01 "s"
ask m: mean(days_between(d0, w) for k in ks)
ask sm: sum(days_between(d0, w) for k in ks)
ask q: quantile(days_between(d0, w) for k in ks, 0.5)
ask x: max(days_between(d0, w) for k in ks)
=== expect
m: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a term of mean" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
q: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a term of quantile" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
sm: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a term of sum" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
x: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for a print" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
